aiGrader.prompt:
Everything you need is in 1.3.6, 1.3.7, 1.3.8 and the worked example in 1.3.10: go back and reread them if you get stuck. A sentence per name is plenty, in your own everyday words.

Here are six variable names. For each one, say whether it is a good name or a bad one, and why: name the rule it follows or breaks. (1.3.6, 1.3.7 and 1.3.8)

  let x = 5;
  let numberOfStudents = 5;
  let d = "Monday";
  let currentDay = "Monday";
  let temp = 98.6;
  let bodyTemperature = 98.6;

Then answer two more:

7. One of those six is genuinely arguable rather than clearly good or clearly bad. Which one, and what makes it arguable? (1.3.8)

8. Match each of these four names: temp, x, a1, myVariable, to its problem: too generic, an abbreviation with no context, a numbered name that says nothing, and meaningless but harmless-sounding. (1.3.7)
